  "text": "Arawn's cauldron points to a parallel with the Dagda, the Irish father god. Arawn had magical pigs, a motif also linked to the Dagda. He handed them over as a present to Pryderi, the mortal king. The bard Gwydion stole the pigs. He was caught and imprisoned in Annwn. Amaethon subsequently carried off three of Arawn's enchanted animals. For one whole year Arawn took the place of the mortal king Pwyll. Pwyll used the time in the Otherworld to kill Hafgan, Arawn's rival for power.",
